\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Condition-specific coverage and common-simplex volume. Small dots are the five held-out seeds; horizontal marks are their means. The dashed line denotes nominal coverage, not a confidence bound. The dotted separator distinguishes response conditions from matched information-removal controls. Compactness and coverage must be read together: shifted Euclidean regions are smaller but under-cover, while boundary ILR regions nearly fill the simplex.}}{6}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:comparison}{{2}{6}{Condition-specific coverage and common-simplex volume. Small dots are the five held-out seeds; horizontal marks are their means. The dashed line denotes nominal coverage, not a confidence bound. The dotted separator distinguishes response conditions from matched information-removal controls. Compactness and coverage must be read together: shifted Euclidean regions are smaller but under-cover, while boundary ILR regions nearly fill the simplex}{figure.caption.6}{}}
